file: "packages/core/src/delta/diff_palette.ts"
doc:
  "The diff render's post-pass: walks a resolved diagram and restyles every element according to its change type.\n"
  "\n"
  "Vocabulary for this file is fixed in delta_overlay.spec.textproto.\n"
  "\n"
  "WHERE THIS RUNS, and why it cannot run earlier. This is a post-pass over an\n"
  "already-resolved diagram. TokenResolverImpl is the last stage of\n"
  "resolvePipeline, so a pass placed before resolvePipeline RETURNS would be\n"
  "handed the literal string \"$roles.node_fill\" where a colour is expected and\n"
  "would try to rotate it.\n"
  "\n"
  "It also cannot run inside StyleCascadeImpl. The cascade has no notion of a\n"
  "Delta, and synthesising diff-coloured elements there would produce elements\n"
  "VisibilityFilterImpl never saw, so the visibility rules would silently not\n"
  "apply to them. The union is built upstream instead, by mergeDelta, and flows\n"
  "through filter, cascade and token resolution as an ordinary Diagram."

methods: [
  { name: "applyDiffPalette"
    doc:
      "A copy of `resolved` with every element restyled for its change type.\n"
      "`resolved` is not mutated.\n"
      "\n"
      "Calls resolveDiffRoles(tokens) ONCE, before the walk, and passes the\n"
      "single result to every recolour call as their `diffRoles` argument.\n"
      "Resolving per element would let one diagram mix table mode and rotate\n"
      "mode, which is the thing resolveDiffRoles's all-or-none rule exists to\n"
      "prevent.\n"
      "\n"
      "Then, for each element, the change type comes from the matching map\n"
      "on `overlay` looked up by the element's own id:\n"
      "  nodes        overlay.nodes\n"
      "  edges        overlay.edges\n"
      "  groups       overlay.groups\n"
      "  annotations  UNCHANGED for every annotation, with no lookup at all\n"
      "               and no map to look in; see DeltaOverlay for why there\n"
      "               is none.\n"
      "\n"
      "and the element's styling is replaced field by field:\n"
      "  ResolvedNode        shape via recolorShape, typography via\n"
      "                      recolorTypography\n"
      "  ResolvedGroup       the same two\n"
      "  ResolvedEdge        connection via recolorLine, typography via\n"
      "                      recolorTypography\n"
      "  ResolvedAnnotation  shape via recolorShape, callout via\n"
      "                      recolorLine, typography via recolorTypography\n"
      "\n"
      "ANNOTATIONS ARE RECOLOURED, not skipped. Passing UNCHANGED through\n"
      "the same three functions means diffColorFor's branch 1 runs, so every\n"
      "colour an annotation carries is DESATURATED, exactly as for an\n"
      "unchanged node. An annotation is commentary on the diagram rather\n"
      "than a part of the graph, so it reads as context, and muted context\n"
      "is what the rest of the unchanged picture looks like too.\n"
      "\n"
      "Every other field of every element -- id, parentGroup, layout, label,\n"
      "content, anchor, isSuperNode, hiddenDescendantCount -- is carried\n"
      "through untouched.\n"
      "\n"
      "`resolved.canvas` is carried through untouched, and the canvas is the\n"
      "one visible surface this function leaves alone. It is the ground the\n"
      "diagram sits on rather than an element that changed, and recolouring\n"
      "it would restyle the whole picture's background for a diff in one\n"
      "corner of it. Annotations sit ON that canvas but are elements with\n"
      "their own styling, which is why the rule above differs from this one.\n"
      "\n"
      "An element whose id is absent from its map is treated as UNCHANGED\n"
      "and must not throw. For an overlay mergeDelta built this cannot\n"
      "happen: the filter and cascade upstream only ever DROP elements, so\n"
      "`resolved` holds a subset of the union diagram's ids and never an id\n"
      "the union lacked. The fallback exists because a DeltaOverlay is an\n"
      "ordinary value a test may build by hand, and a total function is\n"
      "cheaper than a precondition nobody can check."
    inputs: [
      { name: "resolved", type: { named: { symbol: "ResolvedDiagram" } } },
      { name: "overlay",  type: { named: { symbol: "DeltaOverlay" } } },
      { name: "tokens",   type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.theme.v1.Tokens" } }, is_optional: true }
    ]
    output: { named: { symbol: "ResolvedDiagram" } }
    uses: ["resolveDiffRoles", "recolorShape", "recolorLine", "recolorTypography", "archeglyph.content.v1.ChangeType"]
  }
]
